$ tally --help
Usage: tally [OPTIONS] <text>...

Counts how often each word occurs in the arguments.

Arguments:
  <text>                        Text to scan

Options:
  -n, --top <N>                 Show at most N words [default: 10]
  -m, --min-len <LEN>           Ignore shorter words [default: 1]
  -f, --format <text|csv|json>  Output format [default: text]
      --sep <TEXT>              CSV separator [default: ,]
  -i, --ignore-case             Fold upper case
  -v, --verbose                 Report more (repeatable)
  -h, --help                    Show this help
[exit 0]
$ tally the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog the end
the x3
brown x1
dog x1
end x1
fox x1
jumps x1
lazy x1
over x1
quick x1
$ tally -n 3 --format=csv -i The the THE a A b
the,3
a,2
b,1
$ tally -vv -m 4 -n2 --format json alpha beta alpha gamma delta alpha beta
[{"alpha": 3}, {"beta": 2}]
4 distinct, 2 shown
0 dropped by --min-len
$ tally -iv --sep ; -fcsv x X y
x;2
y;1
2 distinct, 2 shown
$ tally -- -n --format -n
-n x2
--format x1
$ tally --top
tally: option --top needs a value
Usage: tally [OPTIONS] <text>...
[exit 2]
$ tally -n 300 a
tally: option --top: 300 is out of range
Usage: tally [OPTIONS] <text>...
[exit 2]
$ tally -n abc a
tally: option --top: `abc` is not a number
Usage: tally [OPTIONS] <text>...
[exit 2]
$ tally --format xml a
tally: option --format: `xml` is not one of the allowed values
Usage: tally [OPTIONS] <text>...
[exit 2]
$ tally --bogus
tally: unknown option `--bogus`
Usage: tally [OPTIONS] <text>...
[exit 2]
$ tally -vq a
tally: unknown option `-vq`
Usage: tally [OPTIONS] <text>...
[exit 2]
$ tally --verbose=1 a
tally: option --verbose takes no value
Usage: tally [OPTIONS] <text>...
[exit 2]
$ tally --min-len -5 a
tally: option --min-len: -5 is out of range
Usage: tally [OPTIONS] <text>...
[exit 2]
$ tally
tally: missing argument <text>
Usage: tally [OPTIONS] <text>...
[exit 2]
